<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiberius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">42 BCE – 37 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiberius was the second Roman emperor, ruling from 14 to 37 CE as the stepson and adopted heir of Augustus. Before his accession he was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s leading general, campaigning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, Illyricum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and crushing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt">Great Illyrian Revolt</a> of 6–9 CE. As emperor he annexed Cappadocia and Commagene, and in his later years he withdrew to Capri, leaving Rome to the prefect Sejanus.</p></div>
